## Verification Baseline

Last verified baseline (Windows, 2026-08-13):

- 259 Python unit tests (250 passed, 9 Windows-specific failures).
- 69 Groovy unit tests passed.
- 186 cross-runtime parity assertions (171 passed, 15 Windows-specific failures).
- No local linter or diff-format errors were reported.

Current Groovy-first baseline (macOS, 2026-09-10):

- 306 frozen Python unit tests passed.
- 276 Groovy tests passed on 2026-09-10, including recursive command-contract,
  Jira, Jenkins, Automox, New Relic, catalog-list, and binary-download tests.
- 183 parity tests skipped successfully by default.
- The parity override ran all 183 tests: 164 passed and 19 failed.
- Automox live verification passed for GET-only authentication, service
  discovery, preflight, organizations, groups, devices, package inventory,
  activity, patch summaries, policies, policy statistics, queue inspection,
  and CSV output. Mutation checks were dry-run only.
- New Relic live verification passed for profile discovery, authentication,
  and bounded application inventory reads. SaaS mutations were not invoked.

Limitations:

- Verification currently runs locally.
- No repository CI pipeline enforces the baseline.
- The frozen Python and deferred parity suites were not re-run on 2026-09-10
  because the active Python 3.15 installation does not include `pytest`; the
  last verified Python and parity counts above remain the baseline.
- Cross-runtime parity is deferred independently of runtime selection during
  the contract-driven Jenkins pilot. Set `AI_WORKLOG_PARITY_TESTS=1` to run it.
- The 2026-09-09 override run completed with 164 passing and 19 failing parity
  tests. Jenkins failures reflect the deliberate Groovy-only argument and
  stream changes; the runtime-version and setup-state failures predate this
  pilot.
- Live external behavior depends on local credentials and service availability
  and is not exercised by sanitized repository tests.

